comments.body:
Trump may turn out to be seen by historians as a push in the right direction for many of the issues he has opposed with his gang that couldn't shoot straight.

The reactions to his Administration's clumsy, idiotic, cruel and inept moves may increase the pace of progress towards the opposite and correct solutions for:

Security--divorcing ourselves from Israel's wars on its neighbors;

Environmental--moving to renewables with more haste;

Financial--making the wealthy carry their fair share of the burden;

And justice--reinforcing democracies and realizing a world determined by a Yalta-like conference of dictators is not acceptable. 

These are solutions we might have fought for years with the old regime to reach.

Who knows, Trump may turn out to be the 21st Century's Christopher Columbus who, until the end of his life, believed he had found the way to Asia.

(Of course, he was ultimately responsible for thousands of deaths and destroying many peaceful nations of Native People mostly willfully.)
